    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0311" n="215" xml:id="pg215"/>

                <head>No. 175.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Case to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy
                                Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 30, 1872</date>.
                        (Received October 31.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Commander Byron Wilson, in a communication
                    dated Gibraltar, October 4, acknowledges the receipt of the Department’s
                    modification of his orders, made at the request of the Secretary of State, to
                    visit Zanzibar instead of Muscat, in the Yantic.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. LUDLOW CASE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of the
                            Navy.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
